# Quant Web Studio — Cursor Rules

## Project overview
Next.js 14 App Router website for Quant Web Studio, a South Wales web design and SEO agency.
Apple-style design: clean, light, minimal. Accent colour #0071e3.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- TypeScript
- CSS Modules (no Tailwind, no styled-components)
- DM Sans font (via next/font/google)
- No external UI libraries

## File structure
src/
  app/
    layout.tsx      — root layout, metadata, JSON-LD schema, fonts
    page.tsx        — homepage (imports all section components)
    globals.css     — design tokens (CSS variables), animations, utilities
    sitemap.ts      — auto-generated sitemap
    robots.ts       — auto-generated robots.txt
  components/
    Nav.tsx / Nav.module.css
    Ticker.tsx / Ticker.module.css
    Hero.tsx / Hero.module.css         (canvas particle animation)
    Stats.tsx / Stats.module.css       (count-up on scroll)
    Services.tsx / Services.module.css
    WhyUs.tsx / WhyUs.module.css       (rank bar animations)
    Location.tsx / Location.module.css
    Faq.tsx / Faq.module.css           (accordion)
    Cta.tsx / Cta.module.css           (contact form)
    Footer.tsx / Footer.module.css
    RevealProvider.tsx                  (scroll reveal IntersectionObserver)
    useReveal.ts

## Design tokens (from globals.css)
--white: #ffffff
--black: #1d1d1f
--gray-1: #f5f5f7   (light backgrounds)
--gray-2: #e8e8ed   (borders, dividers)
--gray-3: #6e6e73   (secondary text)
--gray-4: #86868b   (tertiary text)
--accent: #0071e3   (Apple blue — primary CTA colour)
--accent-dark: #0058b0

## Coding conventions
- Always use CSS Modules for component styles (ComponentName.module.css)
- Client components need 'use client' directive at top
- Server components by default (no directive needed)
- Use Next.js <Link> for internal links, <Image> for images
- All animations via CSS (no animation libraries)
- Scroll reveals use the .reveal CSS class + IntersectionObserver in RevealProvider
- Accessibility: aria-labels on interactive elements, semantic HTML, sr-only labels

## SEO rules
- Every new page needs: title, description, openGraph, twitter metadata via Next.js Metadata API
- JSON-LD schema lives in src/app/layout.tsx — update @graph array for new services/pages
- Add new URLs to src/app/sitemap.ts when creating new pages
- Images: always use next/image with descriptive alt text
- Target keywords: "web design south wales", "SEO agency wales", "web studio cardiff"

## When adding new pages
1. Create src/app/[slug]/page.tsx
2. Add metadata export with title, description, openGraph
3. Add URL to sitemap.ts
4. Add JSON-LD schema if it's a service page

## Contact form
Cta.tsx has a handleSubmit function with a TODO comment.
Replace with Formspree endpoint: POST to https://formspree.io/f/YOUR_FORM_ID
Or use a Next.js API route at src/app/api/contact/route.ts

## Deployment
Target: Vercel (free tier)
Domain: quantweb.co.uk
Run: npm run build — should produce zero errors before deploying
